{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>this time</b><br>By gazelles. Like איל וצבי, and many are masculine, (cf.) וכצבאים על ההרים; and for females: צבאות." "תעירו — from ויעירני." "מקפץ — Targum [of] לנתר." "<b>this time</b><br>And I have sufficiently adjured the maidens not to rouse me from sleep [until the time of love's desire arrives]." "And the sense of בצבאות is that the women are likened to them. Do you not see אילת אהבים ויעלת חן — she is likened to a doe and a gazelle. And this is the sense of השבעתי אתכם — by those likened to you, as though he said: I adjure you by yourselves." "<b>this time</b><br>The prophets said concerning the congregation of Israel: I adjured [you] by gazelles, which are permitted for slaughter, that you not stir until the end arrives, as our Sages of blessed memory transmitted that the sons of Ephraim departed before the end [and this is the sense of עד שתחפץ], and they were killed, and concerning them it is said in Chronicles: ויתאבל עליהם אפרים אביהם."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:01.284042019Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}